          <Comment Type="public">This sequence change replaces cysteine, which is neutral and slightly polar, with tryptophan, which is neutral and slightly polar, at codon 2363 of the RYR1 protein (p.Cys2363Trp). This variant is not present in population databases (gnomAD no frequency). This missense change has been observed in individual(s) with malignant hyperthermia (PMID: 30236257). ClinVar contains an entry for this variant (Variation ID: 478267). Advanced modeling of protein sequence and biophysical properties (such as structural, functional, and spatial information, amino acid conservation, physicochemical variation, residue mobility, and thermodynamic stability) performed at Invitae indicates that this missense variant is expected to disrupt RYR1 protein function. For these reasons, this variant has been classified as Pathogenic.</Comment>
        </Classification>
